                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "77275948-dcd0-3b5f-87dc-8f1321a60427",
                                        "entry_id": "48a977ff-d2c5-35b1-977d-b9f292ed8ec9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any formal system of reasoning that arrives at a truth by the exchange of logical arguments."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "428b8943-f072-3e14-949e-f7c8c13fb667",
                                        "entry_id": "48a977ff-d2c5-35b1-977d-b9f292ed8ec9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A contradiction of ideas that serves as the determining factor in their interaction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf4b1117-07b8-4aea-9a31-d8eab97b5510",
                                                "sense_id": "428b8943-f072-3e14-949e-f7c8c13fb667",
                                                "text": "This situation created the inner dialectic of American history."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8270728f-9f54-32f3-8f2b-e6f777d74c47",
                                        "entry_id": "48a977ff-d2c5-35b1-977d-b9f292ed8ec9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "development by way of overcoming internal contradictions"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Marxism",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dialectic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1fad88e-9ce3-36ba-9773-d87c3b270d1e",
                                        "entry_id": "bec1bb02-2f9a-3ef7-a4ab-aff0d8ad0b15",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dialectical (of or relating to dialectic)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dialectic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "40ad6a85-66b9-3555-92db-432ccfcc1726",
                                        "entry_id": "a49731cb-9542-3e04-907d-7136ebf39e0e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dialectal (of or relating to a dialect)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f5f557f0-7077-495e-863f-ac1d620f0ab6",
                                                "sense_id": "40ad6a85-66b9-3555-92db-432ccfcc1726",
                                                "text": "Is it [prodezza] a mere dialectic variation of prudenza,[…]?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51594468-2351-43eb-87ba-36477f0dec34",
                                                "sense_id": "40ad6a85-66b9-3555-92db-432ccfcc1726",
                                                "text": "[…] if any one has, in common discourse, an indistinct, hesitating, dialectic, or otherwise faulty, delivery, his Natural manner certainly is not what he should adopt in public speaking; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29cf5934-e49a-4c7e-8aaf-81c911d57952",
                                                "sense_id": "40ad6a85-66b9-3555-92db-432ccfcc1726",
                                                "text": "But our able Secretary, Mr. Laidlay, has referred me to another alphabet, dialectic of the Hebrew, as set forth in the interpretation of the bilingual inscription of Thongga (Journal Asiatique, Fevrier, 1843) to which be conceives the characters of this brief specimen may be considered more properly to belong."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70ccb20c-80cd-43c4-9c7d-b1c272c7c595",
                                                "sense_id": "40ad6a85-66b9-3555-92db-432ccfcc1726",
                                                "text": "[…] we have a theory sufficiently consistent with the remote philological relations traceable between Cymri and Gael, and with the close dialectic affinities between Celtic Scotland and Ireland."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3c62f28e-9c79-4cb9-8385-9d1caf979c22",
                        "source_entry_id": "bc159609-280c-30c5-9544-4cc3ab30c35c",
                        "source_sense_id": "4c12ba95-d125-356d-9224-613387c270b4",
                        "source_sense_description": "Philosophie: Methode Schlüsse zu ziehen: These",
                        "target_lang_word": "dialectique",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dialectique",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "689663a7-9818-3c7c-8e14-7a8b4d5cef7b",
                                        "entry_id": "a637918e-8792-357b-8cd8-7f3502f9f22a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui a rapport aux règles du raisonnement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46cb3134-df70-47ed-9f1e-67efdd7eee90",
                                                "sense_id": "689663a7-9818-3c7c-8e14-7a8b4d5cef7b",
                                                "text": "Les procédés dialectiques."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "879f93d5-55a4-4bd4-8a33-2128fcfc7f51",
                                                "sense_id": "689663a7-9818-3c7c-8e14-7a8b4d5cef7b",
                                                "text": "Habité par les idées de Hegel, Miguel de Unamuno établit une opposition dialectique entre les deux personnages. Sancho est la projection de Quichotte vers la réalité, comme Quichotte demeure l’idéal respecté de Sancho."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24d63fdb-2be3-4573-b509-9ce90a53f09e",
                                                "sense_id": "689663a7-9818-3c7c-8e14-7a8b4d5cef7b",
                                                "text": "Un modèle fécond permet ainsi de faire progresser la recherche dans un champ scientifique en engendrant un mouvement dialectique entre la théorie et l’expérimentation. — (Lionel Naccache, Le Nouvel Inconscient : Freud, le Christophe Colomb des neurosciences, Odile Jacob, 2009, page 265)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dialectique",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f44ba1f-0b38-398b-a920-bd7e0a315cfb",
                                        "entry_id": "c715ea50-c978-32d3-979a-23d8ba42fc0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Méthode de raisonnement, de questionnement et d’interprétation qui consiste à analyser la réalité en mettant en évidence les contradictions de celle-ci tout en cherchant à les dépasser."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8eb5afde-1e61-4f1d-9158-58f15fe91688",
                                                "sense_id": "0f44ba1f-0b38-398b-a920-bd7e0a315cfb",
                                                "text": "Aristote attribue à Zénon d'Élée d'être l'inventeur de la dialectique."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41fc11e3-1817-4895-b86b-4dd34f20c75f",
                                                "sense_id": "0f44ba1f-0b38-398b-a920-bd7e0a315cfb",
                                                "text": "On rencontre bien, de temps à autre, des tentatives isolées d’appliquer la dialectique, c’est-à-dire la démonstration rationnelle, aux questions religieuses : […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5300fa3-0966-41d6-974f-80464b515274",
                                                "sense_id": "0f44ba1f-0b38-398b-a920-bd7e0a315cfb",
                                                "text": "La dialectique était la première partie de la philosophie scolastique."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfdb4f30-c571-44e7-b2d3-c202dd279424",
                                                "sense_id": "0f44ba1f-0b38-398b-a920-bd7e0a315cfb",
                                                "text": "Dialectique serrée, pressante, subtile, ingénieuse, spécieuse."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9797d23-833b-3578-a34e-6ad5c133b355",
                                        "entry_id": "c715ea50-c978-32d3-979a-23d8ba42fc0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Suite de raisonnements rigoureux visant à emporter l’adhésion de son interlocuteur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee7755fb-12e4-3d41-97c6-bdbcf8695499",
                                        "entry_id": "c715ea50-c978-32d3-979a-23d8ba42fc0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dynamique relationnelle caractérisée par un va-et-vient entre deux positions, chacune influençant l'autre à tour de rôle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1d73a34-09d7-4a5c-ba30-ac570ca0dfa0",
                                                "sense_id": "ee7755fb-12e4-3d41-97c6-bdbcf8695499",
                                                "text": "Le changement n'est donc pas quelque chose qui puisse être imposé sur le monde unilatéralement. Il est dialogue, dialectique, aller-retour.."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
